{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses","id":791114,"title":"[Changeling: The Lost 2E Teaser]New Seeming Blessings and Curses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-22T15:13:52-08:00","id":791114,"title":"[Changeling: The Lost 2E Teaser]New Seeming Blessings and Curses","content":"Hey guys! Exciting times abound!<br /> <br /> So, some news about how things are going first. First, Changeling's Second Edition has started kicking off again, with David blowing through a lot of the Redlines in the last week. It's the holiday season, so the writer's are understandably are working around that, but all in all, Changeling Second is starting to move again. So keep up the hope-we're not out of the woods, but we're starting to see the lights of home as far as writing goes.<br /> <br /> Second, I got hired for the Changeling Second's core book. Thanks go to David for the opportunity, and you all for your support. We hope you'll enjoy our work. What am I adding? You'll find out, if you don't already know.<br /> <br /> Was there a third? Can't recall, must not be. SO, enough of that, let's get to what you all want. It's been a bit of a drought of news for CtL 2E, and NDA keeps me from spoiling <i>new</i> things, but I've got a go ahead to talk about clarified old things, which in this case means the redlined Seeming Blessings and Curses.<br /> <br /> Changeling is a game of transformations, where narratives become lives, bad memories become storm clouds, and promises become flesh. Metaphors run the risk of becoming literal truths as far as the fae are concerned, and changelings with Seemings are more aware of that than most. Seeming's, as an expression of reclaiming agency, both freed and cursed changelings, giving them stability within the niche role they've crafted for themselves but destroying their Clarity when their freedom is challenged. With this, some of the original blessings and curses had expanded additions, such as the Beast's curse with restraints or the Wizened's blessings of perfection. Many of you voiced concern that this might not have been enough, and David listened to those concerns. Because, yes, that is right. A Seeming, as a promise in a world where heartfelt words and actions becomes mountains and storms, should be more than a tool to help you see the world and yourself clearly-it should be empowering. After all, you told the Wyrd you would be powerful, and so the Wyrd will <i>make</i> you powerful...at a price, of course.<br /> <br /> Here, then, are the redlined suggestions for Seeming's Blessing and Curses, with the mechanical benefits bolded for ease of finding. Keep in mind that these are still in production and subject to change as it transitions over into the second drafts. Dave has just added his notes of what he thinks should be added and refined, nothing's actually been rewritten yet. We also have some curses missing. Dave and Filamena are still mulling over stuff. Still, we think you'll like what you'll see.<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Blessing - Clarity of Abandon:</b> Lost in the lies and oppression of society, a Beast has great difficulty making head or tales of the cultural landscape before her. She remembers, though vaguely, that there is a reason for many of the rules and laws that keep people civilized, but the importance of those reasons has faded away. Rules of society are only chains around her neck, and obedience to those old ways is suffocating. (Perhaps suffocating to everyone, but only the Beast is wise enough to notice.) Once per story, a Beast can flaunt a cultural taboo despite great personal cost, and regain a point of Clarity for free. <b>Additionally, she never suffers penalties to her dice pools in pursuit, whether she is the hunter or the prey.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Curse - A Beast\u2019s Burden:</b> Confinement is a fate worse than death to the Beast. She\u2019s experienced it already, and her spirit is simply too big to fit comfortably into bondage. A Beast can, of her own free will, enter into a Contract or Pledge or other more intimate acts of binding, but it chafes her more than the average Lost. Forced confinement, especially the physical kind, is too much for her. <b>Escaping bonds requires three Glamour instead of one.</b> Once per story, if a Beast is confined or imprisoned, she suffers a Clarity breaking point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Darklings</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Blessing - Clarity of Abandon:</b> At times, the best choice is the worst choice. Any time a Darkling is forced to step in and make a bad choice for others, to make the choice no one else could, she gains a sense of herself. She regains a point of Clarity for free. The Storyteller should machinate these sorts of situations about once a story, as much as it is a Darkling\u2019s tendency to seek out these situations for herself. <b>Additionally, a Darkling never suffers penalties to her senses in the dark. She cannot see through a blindfold, but she can see perfectly with no light whatsoever.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Curse - A Shade\u2019s Distrust:</b> A Darkling has been injured in the past, and believes she\u2019s injured others to survive. A Darkling trusted once, a long time ago, and anyone asking her to trust may be pushing her too hard. Trusting anyone, even a Darklings\u2019 closest allies, following them blindly, causes the Darkling to suffer a Clarity break.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> *A life curse is still being mulled over. Suggestions are welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Elementals</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Blessing - Clarity of Forces:</b> Elementals appear to be creatures of whim and devastation, burning bridges, throwing caution to the wind, and storming through life without a thought or concern. That\u2019s not exactly true, as the Elemental knows instinctively, their chaos has a pattern, and there\u2019s order behind the destruction. Once per story, when the player of an Elemental can bring meaning and purpose to what appeared to be an act of pure chaos earlier in the story, that character gains a point of Clarity for free. The player did not have to be planning for this meaning at the time the character created the chaos; she can retroactively attribute her role, and thus her responsibility. <b>Additionally, Elementals suffer no direct harm from their embodied element. This is at Storyteller discretion. But for example, an Elemental of fire might be able to walk through a burning building, but still risks asphyxiation. For more conceptual Elementals, work out just what this Blessing means, and its limitations. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Curse - Burning Without Ego:</b> To Escape, the Elemental needed release his ego and become one with the force he accepted into himself. The freedom to be without self often means forgetting that others still cling to superficial notions like \u201cme,\u201d and \u201cnow\u201d. Therefore, whenever an Elemental is confronted with the damage in her wake, and sees a good example that not everyone is a raw force like she is, it\u2019s a breaking point. <b>Additionally, cold iron, in its ability to make the ethereal static, is particularly harmful to the Elemental. Any time she is injured by cold iron, she suffers an additional and specific Condition unique to her elemental nature. So, an ice Elemental may choose that her character also becomes Lethargic when hit by cold iron. An Elemental of wind might become Spooked after a cold iron injury. This Condition should be picked at character creation, but can be changed through play as if it were an Aspiration.</b> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Fairest</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Blessing - Clarity of the Crown:</b> The truth of leadership is this: Sometimes it\u2019s not about being right, it\u2019s about appearing right. It\u2019s about appearing right, even when there is no real right or wrong. It isn\u2019t pretty, and it\u2019s certainly a quick path to corruption, but it remains true regardless. Most people need to be led, and when they\u2019re scared or desperate, they\u2019re naturally going to turn to the Fairest. It\u2019s the easy choice. And since so many are naturally going to put themselves in the hands of the Fairest, the Fairest has to do something, anything. Any time a Fairest bluffs, blusters, or shoots from the hip on her way through a call for leadership, and find her self revived by it. Once per story, a Fairest can feel her way through, and she gains a point of Clarity for free. <b>Additionally, a Fairest does not suffer penalties to her Presence or Manipulation dice pools (but Resisted traits still penalize her pools); for her, a little mud on her face just makes her look that much more genuine and stately. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Curse - Weight of the Righteous:</b> With measured response and skill, or blind luck and hope, making the right choice feels damn good. But sooner or later, failure weighs on the Fairest, and the crown on her head gets heavier and heavier. Any time a Fairest makes a call as a leader, and someone gets seriously hurt physically or otherwise, is a breaking point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> *There's plans on making the Fairest easier to find for the Huntsmen. At the time of this redline, Huntsmen's abilities to find particular changeling's were not refined and figured out. The Huntsmen have since been redlined, so there will be probably be a return to this plan.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogres</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Blessing - Clarity of Violence:</b> Ogres aren\u2019t especially good at communicating with words. There are some ideas only her fists can communicate. Once per Story, if an Ogre can manage to get a message across through the use or threat of violence, she gains a point of Clarity for Free. <b>Additionally, an Ogre never suffers wound penalties (see p. XX). However, for this reason she only gains a Beat if her final Health box is filled (see p. XX). </b><br /> <br /> <b>Curse - Hurt People Hurt People:</b> Despite his outward appearance and insistence otherwise, an Ogre does feel pain just like anyone else. So, when someone else can prove to him or those who know him well that something is causing him real pain, it\u2019s a breaking point. This breaking point only happens once per any specific source for the pain. So, after some heavy conversation and a lot of beers, an ex boyfriend tells an Ogre that his real problem is that he never forgive his parents for dying, and it\u2019s a breaking point. Bringing up those dead parents again won\u2019t do it. However, pointing out that he\u2019s broken his fist in a fight about the honor of his dead mother, that\u2019s a new breaking point.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> *A life curse is still being mulled over. Suggestions are welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Blessing - Clarity of Comfort:</b> Her special gift has been and will always be the place she can go to in order to feel safe, to recover, to recoup. Choose a Skill when making your Wizened. Once per story, when she runs away from the world, avoiding problems by using her gift as a means of self comfort she regains a Clarity point. <b>When focused on her craft, she is unshakable. She suffers no penalties when acting with her chosen Skill. This does not limit Defense or Resisted traits, but she suffers no penalties from distraction, her environment, limited time, or stress.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Curse - The Problem with Perfection:</b> The line between genius and perfection is thin, and the considerable talent that Wizened have devoted himself to can also consume him. Any time a Wizened fails an action related to his unique talent, it\u2019s a breaking point. This does not have to be a roll for direct performance (and in fact, usually isn\u2019t); for example, a painter may fail in procuring a very specific pigment, and suffer, or a politician might suffer a scandal that hurts her poll numbers, or a fencer breaks her weapon on the way to a duel.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> *The curse currently being played with is something to do with Hegdespun and Tokens. Tokens had not been reviewed yet at the time of this redline. They have since been redlined, so there will probably be a return to this-I'm thinking an additional Glamour to Tokens that don't relate to the Wizened's chosen Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-22-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T15:19:04-08:00","id":791117,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there some talk about clarifying the Fairest Curse so it's only a Breaking Point if people get hurt unintentionally? A literal reading right now means it's a breaking point to tell your knights to beat up that loyalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T15:20:30-08:00","id":791120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=791117#post791117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there some talk about clarifying the Fairest Curse so it's only a Breaking Point if people get hurt unintentionally? A literal reading right now means it's a breaking point to tell your knights to beat up that loyalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording is still being mulled over. This note is in the comments on the page.<br /> <br /> Keeping things simple here, for the purposes of showcasing stuff. That said, again, keep in mind that Redlines here means &quot;Editor's Proofwriting/Copywriting&quot;. This is Dave going over stuff with a red pen. The Blessings and some of the curses we have are him writing in the margins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-22-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T15:52:08-08:00","id":791133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses#post791114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys! Exciting times abound!<br /> <br /> So, some news about how things are going first. First, Changeling's Second Edition has started kicking off again, with David blowing through a lot of the Redlines in the last week. It's the holiday season, so the writer's are understandably are working around that, but all in all, Changeling Second is starting to move again. So keep up the hope-we're not out of the woods, but we're starting to see the lights of home as far as writing goes.<br /> <br /> Second, I got hired for the Changeling Second's core book. Thanks go to David for the opportunity, and you all for your support. We hope you'll enjoy our work. What am I adding? You'll find out, if you don't already know.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very good to hear. And congrats for being hired for the core! I look forward to seeing your touch in the pages.<br /> <br /> I'm liking the mechanical benefits shown here. They feel fitting to the Seeming themes and useful relative to their niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-22-2015, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:13:40-08:00","id":791188,"title":"","content":"Darkling, the first thing to come to mind is something that makes it harder for other people to heal the darkling. Also, with the blessing, is it that you don't ever take penalties to sight from being in the dark or that you never suffers penalties to her senses in the dark? Does this allow you to ignore penalties to hearing while in darkness?<br /> <br /> Ogre, I don't think the name of the curse fits right now since it doesn't promote the hurt individual hurting others by accident. So perhaps something that makes dramatic failures with socialize or empathy rolls more likely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-22-2015, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T22:27:52-08:00","id":791341,"title":"","content":"I've a got a small suggestion,it would be nice if both the vurses and the belessings become strongers when changeling's wyrd rises","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T23:01:12-08:00","id":791357,"title":"","content":"For Beasts - how strictly do you want to define the word pursuit. Do you literally mean following and chasing, or could it be a looser use of the word? Flirting with an individual you desire as a mate, tracking down a lost or valuable object, seeking the answer to a riddle or trying to lobby a senator to make a particular decision before a rival can influence them in the opposite way could all be considered a pursuit, and I'm okay with that. I'm just curious as to what the intent is. I actually like it. It leaves it open to things like this:<br /> <br /> Ares stalked through the stacks, and the few students who bothered to look up from their studies saw that his nostrils were flared in irritation. What they saw, of course, was the human illusion. Ares' real nostrils were at the end of a bull's snout, his spiked hair truely horns that could gore a grown man. The clerks said that information on the real Yellow Sign was obscure and hard to come by, even in the Killiam's vast stacks. They didn't understand it though. With over a million tomes, the library was a labyrinth. It was his labyrinth. If the information was here, he would find it, and damned be those who get in his way. <br /> <br /> I think that's very beastly, and it adds a lot of potential ways that a beast might make use of that advantage, be it physically, intellectually, or socially. A variety of character ideas is a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T08:24:16-08:00","id":791603,"title":"","content":"Given the new chase rules and how they can be applied to social chases?<br /> <br /> Keep it open man, keep them Beasts sexy. But I don't write the Seemings, so that might not be what Dave had in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-23-2015, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T10:54:27-08:00","id":791681,"title":"","content":"I think the Darkling curse should be something to do with Pledges (maybe they're more expensive to create). <br /> <br /> As far as Ogres go, I think something to do with social maneuvering. Since they don't acknowledge their own vulnerability, they have a harder time empathizing with others so they can be overly judgemental or carelessly hurtful. Maybe they start one impression level lower or have to overcome more doors (except when using hard leverage). Alternately, their belief in their own invulnerability could make them easy to goad or taunt into action.<br /> <br /> So what was the curse or blessing mechanic that surprised you, ArcaneArts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T10:57:47-08:00","id":791686,"title":"","content":"So, way back when the Darklings came out, there was a new forumite called princeofcincinatti or some such who kept saying that Darklings should be able to see in the dark. I told him that was missing the point.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I happen to like raw egg, so I can stand having some on my face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T10:45:12-08:00","id":792248,"title":"","content":"Well, it;s probably a little less fitting <i>now</i>, given how Darklings' link to shadow is metaphorical these days...<br /> <br /> But then again, not by much; they've faced their own darkness with open eyes, they've learned the trick of ignoring normal absence of light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T11:27:14-08:00","id":792268,"title":"","content":"No wounds penalties is a hell of advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T17:17:22-08:00","id":792441,"title":"","content":"The Orgers blessing is a double edged sword, he or she loses out on beats, which helps balance out ignoring wound penalties.<br /> <br /> I like CSSchulz's idea for Darklings' curse, boosting the cost of making a pledge fits the Darkling's trust issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T17:29:14-08:00","id":792445,"title":"","content":"BTW Congrats Arcane, that's outstanding! I'm happy to know your on the core book team, I can see your passion for Changeling the Lost in your posts and I'm sure it will add extra vitality to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:44:50-08:00","id":792471,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now, back to getting it in on time. @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T22:12:54-08:00","id":792558,"title":"","content":"Darkling:<br /> <i>&quot;</i><i>Darkling has been injured in the past, and believes she\u2019s injured others to survive.&quot;</i> - So maybe severe Wound penalties, as Darkling seeing that &quot;everybody can bleed&quot;, them especially? They whole Escape was about survival and pragmatism, so their Curse is about them becoming even more fragile. Mine proposition is this - Their Wound penalties goes up to -4, not -3 like normal.<br /> <br /> I would not mess with Pledges and Oaths as they are really big thing in <b>Changeling</b> game - if you made them limited here, you will see not very often Darkling Pledge Crafters - and by their Escape story, they should be <i>best</i> ones, not worst ones, in 2ED setting.<br /> <br /> Ogres:<br /> I agree with idea on one extra Door in Social Maneuvering - it sounds appropriate for Brutes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T22:35:34-08:00","id":792582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=792558#post792558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darkling:<br /> <i>&quot;</i><i>Darkling has been injured in the past, and believes she\u2019s injured others to survive.&quot;</i> - So maybe severe Wound penalties, as Darkling seeing that &quot;everybody can bleed&quot;, them especially? They whole Escape was about survival and pragmatism, so their Curse is about them becoming even more fragile. Mine proposition is this - Their Wound penalties goes up to -4, not -3 like normal.<br /> <br /> I would not mess with Pledges and Oaths as they are really big thing in <b>Changeling</b> game - if you made them limited here, you will see not very often Darkling Pledge Crafters - and by their Escape story, they should be <i>best</i> ones, not worst ones, in 2ED setting.<br /> <br /> Ogres:<br /> I agree with idea on one extra Door in Social Maneuvering - it sounds appropriate for Brutes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like that idea for the Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T23:46:54-08:00","id":792627,"title":"","content":"Beasts:<br /> Does all changelings can free themselves with 1 Glamour? I still thinks that some Social penalties would be better idea as they are &quot;wild&quot; inside and out. Maybe they have one Door less in Social Maneuvering when acting on their Vice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T06:38:27-08:00","id":792726,"title":"","content":"Well, first, I must say that I'm enchanted about what had transpired for now. I'm highly excited about this new edition and I can't wait to play with it.<br /> <br /> Now, more precisely:<br /> - Beasts: The mechanics seem both powerful and fulfilling for this one. I like it.<br /> - Darklings: I could see something about the Darkling needing some extra points of Glamour for entering into a Plegde, or maybe that they could suffer from a negative Condition when dealing particular important Oaths.<br /> - Elementals: Nothing to say here, it seems good.<br /> - Fairest: I like the Sidhe feelings of the Blessing. It's difficult to ridiculise someone who never stop appearing regal and royal even after receiving a cream pie in the face. For the Curse, I like the whole &quot;easier to find&quot; stuff but I think it should apply to anyone trying to find the Fairest. It's not easy being a protagonist after all, and not only for escaping the Huntsmen. All your past lovers, they always seems to find you. Your maniacally morbid Fetche, all the same. The guy you punched in the bar last night, as expected. You impressed the Wyrd by becoming important in other people's lives, the Wyrd will make sure that it will never be different.<br /> - Ogres: I have no idea but the propositions about them dealing bad socially seems fine to me.<br /> - Wizened: For the Curse, I could see something about them needing to spend a Willpower point for stopping an extended roll before the last roll. It makes more sense to me as a Perfection problem that the Token's one who seems to deal with overwhelming Specialization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T15:35:49-08:00","id":792850,"title":"","content":"With darkling's and pledges, it could be something like minor backlash to the changeling if the other party fails to hold up their end of the pledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:06:44-08:00","id":793122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=792850#post792850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With darkling's and pledges, it could be something like minor backlash to the changeling if the other party fails to hold up their end of the pledge.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that, the Darkling took the risk of trusting someone else and got burned, which remains them of a past betrayal, so maybe they suffer a condition when someone breaks a pledge with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:15:34-08:00","id":793126,"title":"","content":"Boosting the effect of Seemings will also make the Fae Touched more interesting.<br /> <br /> So a Fae Touched Darkling will be able to see in the dark, a Fae Touched Fairest will be able to ignore social penalties other then resistance, ect...<br /> <br /> This I assume will also extend to Grimms, Loyalists, and the other Seeming.<br /> <br /> It just occured to me that their could be Loyalist Fae Touched who never had any Loyalty to the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:24:09-08:00","id":793140,"title":"","content":"Had something of a parkour master beast in mind, and I'm divided between toning it down so that he can actually benefit from that chase part of the blessing, or if I should keep it at full tilt. NPCs need inescapable horrors, too, after all. &gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:36:21-08:00","id":793146,"title":"","content":"Everyone does.<br /> <br /> Fun fact of Changeling: there always will be, for PC's and NPC's.<br /> <br /> Can't outrun a story. Or can you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:02:30-08:00","id":793165,"title":"","content":"Seeming Curses and Blessings need to make sense for both Changels &amp; Fae Touched, so far example of Wizen need to spend 2 glamour to use a hedge spun took instead of one, that doesn't work right on a FaeTouched as they can't spend their Glamour on activating a Hedge Spun Token so either that or the curse itself has to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T17:01:42-08:00","id":793320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=793146#post793146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone does.<br /> <br /> Fun fact of Changeling: there always will be, for PC's and NPC's.<br /> <br /> Can't outrun a story. Or can you?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't know, ask <a href=\"http://www.comicvine.com/loki-agent-of-asgard/4050-71432/\" target=\"_blank\">Loki.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:38:54-08:00","id":793365,"title":"","content":"For Ogres Curse, what about<b></b>: <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Choose a condition that represents the state in which you're most vulnerable. It may be a positive or a negative condition, as you wish. You may also create a new condition with your storyteller.<br /> <br /> For example: Connected, Lost, Swooned, Informed, Guilty, Spooken.<br /> (there should be also some condition about &quot;being too vain&quot;, &quot;hungry&quot; or &quot;enraged&quot;) <br /> <br /> When you have such condition, or a similar one, your heart is vulnerable - every social roll against you has a +3 bonus (or, you lose your defense, or, every hit does +1 damage.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T09:22:48-08:00","id":796862,"title":"","content":"Re: Darklings and Pledges:<br /> Forgive me if I'm wrong, but shouldn't Darklings, as people with serious trust issues, be <i>more</i> likely than other Changelings to make pledges? To a Darkling, a pledge would replace the need to trust. Knowing that there are consequences if the other party betrays them should be a balm to the Darkling. I'd say that rather than making it harder to make pledges, a Darkling should have penalties when dealing with people whom they <i>hadn't</i> made a pledge with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:30:42-08:00","id":797087,"title":"","content":"That makes sense, a pledge would give them a sense of security from betrayal.<br /> <br /> How about a penalty in daylight to their magic, like using magic in the day costs an extra glamour or would that be too costly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T01:20:56-08:00","id":797232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses#post791114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I got hired for the Changeling Second's core book. Thanks go to David for the opportunity, and you all for your support. We hope you'll enjoy our work. What am I adding? You'll find out, if you don't already know.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations! Always nice to see a fan working on something they love.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T07:55:52-08:00","id":797348,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing these, Arc! This is certainly something to chew over. The Elemental blessing caught me off-guard at first, primarily because if I recall the Elemental Hunterheart is described as being made of weapons and traps, but I guess that's what gives the phrase &quot;Storyteller discretion&quot; its deserved tenure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T10:23:13-08:00","id":797410,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of power in the Storyteller's ability to just say &quot;No, that's stupid.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T10:40:35-08:00","id":797415,"title":"","content":"The Darkling curse concerns me. Like... Old CTD Pooka always lies concerns. Just because I can see a lot of people using it as an excuse to never be team players at all. It just feels like a bad thing for roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T14:40:52-08:00","id":797513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=797415#post797415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Darkling curse concerns me. Like... Old CTD Pooka always lies concerns. Just because I can see a lot of people using it as an excuse to never be team players at all. It just feels like a bad thing for roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm my opinion this should not really occur, simply because it only happens if you trust and follow someone &quot;Blindly&quot;. If you have proper justifications, then it doesn't occur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:02:15-08:00","id":797785,"title":"","content":"If you go to a sturgeon and just trusted his or her word and let them operate on you, that would trigger the Darklings curse, because your blindly trusting the surgeon, but if you looked up the surgeons creditials first, got a second opinion, looked up testimonials from previous patients, and got a lawyer ready in case the surgeon botched, then its not blind trust and the Darklings curse wouldn't activate.<br /> <br /> Its comes down to having some measure of control in every situation because you don't trust people anymore.<br /> <br /> That control could take the form of researching somebody (to the point of stalking potentially), having a plan B if shit goes wrong, doing things for yourself instead of trusting others to do it for you, being manipulative, whatever makes the Darkling feel protected from betrayal.<br /> <br /> And different Darklings might go about there paranoia in different ways, a Romantic or Illes Darkling might manipulate allies so that the Darkling believe they won't betray the Darkling because that Darkling has his/her claws in them.<br /> <br /> A Woodblood Darkling might just perfer avoiding relying on anyone at all period.<br /> <br /> A Darkling Antiqarian might do research on the people around them to make sure they're qualified as they claim to be.<br /> <br /> A Darkling Draconic might talk about the nasty shit they did to those who betrayed them around they're friends dropping a hint about consquences.<br /> <br /> A gravewright Darkling might get Ghosts to spy on and test their allies or anyone they have to trust, so it won't be blind trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:06:16-08:00","id":797789,"title":"","content":"Also I can see Darklings being the most likely to violate their curse knowingly and on purpose either out of love or as a function of their blessing in otherwords if risking their clarity and betraying themselves is the lesser evil in a situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T17:47:47-08:00","id":798038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=797415#post797415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Darkling curse concerns me. Like... Old CTD Pooka always lies concerns. Just because I can see a lot of people using it as an excuse to never be team players at all. It just feels like a bad thing for roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, that's like saying Humanity is the reason Vampire characters never kill anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Me