ode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=800542#post800542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess David and his team have had a wonderful burst of productivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just got back in the saddle after some shit. Was hospitalised for a while. But, it's all moving along now. I'm sad I'm not further along with Changeling than I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T08:11:06-08:00","id":803097,"title":"","content":"I don't really like Ogre's ability to ignore wound penalties. It's nice mechanically but the same effect can be gained by takin Iron Stamina 3 Merit, something that everyone can do. All other Seemings gain something unique, so I would like to see something for Ogres that can't replicated by single Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:49:58-08:00","id":803374,"title":"","content":"David what matters most is that your okay, we can be patient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T03:07:19-08:00","id":809469,"title":"","content":"So now that we have rules for the Huntsmen, I have wondered how the Fairest Curse will interact with them. It seems a little odd and overkill to me to make such masters of the hunt even better when chasing a Fairest quarry, especially since the Hunstmen are antagonists. It's just that generally speaking, I doesn't make sense to me to make rolls with an enemy who hasn't be introduced yet. If I wanted to introduced a Huntsman in my chronicles, I would want to make it appear where and when I want. Especially since it's repeatedly stated the Huntsmen are incredibly driven by narration.<br /> <br /> I have two suggestions:<br /> - what if the Fairest were considered by all Huntsmen as a prospective target. What if all Huntsmen, even the ones who weren't designed to hunt them, could take a Fairest to his master and be considered successful. It make sense since the Fairest are protagonists and all. The problem here is that it diffuses the tension of the hunt for other changelings.<br /> - alternatively, what if it was tougher for Fairests to make deal with the Huntsmen. What if they couldn't collect Tokens of Reprieve of their own as easily as other changelings. After all, they became Fairests because they extended and reached out a hand, it should be difficult for them to betray fellow changelings, even if the changeling in question is a sworn enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:35:01-08:00","id":809742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=809469#post809469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now that we have rules for the Huntsmen, I have wondered how the Fairest Curse will interact with them. It seems a little odd and overkill to me to make such masters of the hunt even better when chasing a Fairest quarry, especially since the Hunstmen are antagonists. It's just that generally speaking, I doesn't make sense to me to make rolls with an enemy who hasn't be introduced yet. If I wanted to introduced a Huntsman in my chronicles, I would want to make it appear where and when I want. Especially since it's repeatedly stated the Huntsmen are incredibly driven by narration.<br /> <br /> I have two suggestions:<br /> - what if the Fairest were considered by all Huntsmen as a prospective target. What if all Huntsmen, even the ones who weren't designed to hunt them, could take a Fairest to his master and be considered successful. It make sense since the Fairest are protagonists and all. The problem here is that it diffuses the tension of the hunt for other changelings.<br /> - alternatively, what if it was tougher for Fairests to make deal with the Huntsmen. What if they couldn't collect Tokens of Reprieve of their own as easily as other changelings. After all, they became Fairests because they extended and reached out a hand, it should be difficult for them to betray fellow changelings, even if the changeling in question is a sworn enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like the second one a lot more, but a Seeming is permanent, so players might hesitate to play a Fairest it if comes with that kind of drawback. Huntsmen sound like they should be feared by all Seemings in equal measure.<br /> <br /> Here are my suggestions:<br /> <br /> <b>Ogres:</b> I have to agree that immunity to wound penalties doesn't cut it as a Seeming Blessing. Not every Ogre gets into combat all the time, and there's room for scientist and scholar Ogres who solve problems with cold, calculating reason. I believe they should get a greater resistance against not only Social Maneuvering, but also mind-affecting powers that may destabilize their callous hearts. Again, this greater resistance should go beyond universally available Merits like Iron Will and Indomitable. Their affinity for Stone is not just about breaking bones, but also about the Sticks-And-Stones saying.<br /> <br /> <b>Elementals:</b> I am very leery of letting players retroactively declare heat-of-the-moment decisions as clever plans, even with the caveat of their Curse. I figured Elementals in 2ED would still suffer some kind of Social penalty, though the devs appear to be moving away from that kind of drawback. I am also very glad to see that immunity to harmful manifestations of their chosen element is now an inherent advantage of the Seeming, rather than a meager scene-long boost to Health that only becomes useful at high Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> I believe what defines this Seeming is not specialization, but perfectionism, so a Curse that limits their capacity to use and craft Tokens doesn't sound appealing to me. If I play a Wizened, I'd like the option to eventually adopt a new talent to define myself (perhaps with a different Kith along the way), and the possibility to become the closest thing to a fae polymath or Mr. Fixit that I can. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/LoopholeAbuse\" target=\"_blank\"><b>There ain't no rule</b></a> saying that versatility can't be my defining talent, is there? I know perfecting versatility is more about broadness in skills rather than any actual perfection, but I'm sure you got my point.<br /> <br /> Also, I assume that coming across a situation that triggers their Curses calls for a roll, rather than immediately dropping their Clarity. What kind of circumstantial modifiers have been discussed for this roll, if any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-16-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T12:18:16-08:00","id":809780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=809742#post809742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M<b>Elementals:</b> I am very leery of letting players retroactively declare heat-of-the-moment decisions as clever plans, even with the caveat of their Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the whole point is that they're not declaring them as clever plans. They're saying &quot;See? Good *can* come of me acting impulsively in the heat of the moment!&quot; and that reinforces their sense of agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T06:33:51-08:00","id":810207,"title":"","content":"For Wizen I'd give them obsessive compulsive disorder condition for a curse instead of the token thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:57:44-08:00","id":810648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=803097#post803097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really like Ogre's ability to ignore wound penalties. It's nice mechanically but the same effect can be gained by takin Iron Stamina 3 Merit, something that everyone can do. All other Seemings gain something unique, so I would like to see something for Ogres that can't replicated by single Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. An effect that can be gained by anyone for three Experiences seems a little light for a Blessing, especially since it makes it harder for the Ogre to gain Beats as well. What if instead of removing wound penalties, it changed them into bonuses? The Ogres could still gain Beats as normal, and it would make them far more dangerous as they got closer to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T09:38:15-08:00","id":810662,"title":"","content":"that kills some of the wrecking ball toughness we'd want.<br /> <br /> Armor of some level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T11:07:28-08:00","id":810696,"title":"","content":"Armor would be a little redondant with a huge number of Kith's Blessings. Extra Health seems safer for me. It was even a bonus Ogres could achieved from the Evolution of the Wyrd rules in The Equinox Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:34:54-08:00","id":810790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=810662#post810662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that kills some of the wrecking ball toughness we'd want.<br /> <br /> Armor of some level?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think that turning their penalties into bonuses would increase the toughness of Ogres, but I guess I can see where you're coming from with it. Taking away the wound penalties makes it seem like Ogres are capable of enduring a lot, while that endurance could easily be overlooked if the penalties became bonuses, since the focus would end up on their increased attack power instead. Thinking purely on the defensive side, what if their Defense didn't decrease due to multiple opponents? If that seems too potent, it could be limited to a number of additional attackers equal to their Wyrd. The extra Health that DaemonChrno suggested could also work, perhaps by adding their Wyrd to their Health levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T16:39:44-08:00","id":810871,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna have to share a big concern: it seems the mechanics for gaining and losing Clarity reinforce bad or at least questionable behaviors. I am probably looking at it the wrong way, though. Can someone offer their own point of view?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T17:33:07-08:00","id":810883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=810871#post810871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna have to share a big concern: it seems the mechanics for gaining and losing Clarity reinforce bad or at least questionable behaviors. I am probably looking at it the wrong way, though. Can someone offer their own point of view?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, have the Clarity mechanics been spoiled yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T18:40:19-08:00","id":810901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=810883#post810883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, have the Clarity mechanics been spoiled yet?</div> </div> </div> </div> Oops, sorry. I was referring to the ways of gaining and losing Clarity specific to each Seeming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:18:02-08:00","id":810911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=810901#post810901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oops, sorry. I was referring to the ways of gaining and losing Clarity specific to each Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Gotcha. In retrospect that should have been obvious. I'm just overeager to see the Clarity rules spoiled.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not exactly sure what you mean by questionable behaviors. Could you give an example of what it is you're concerned the Clarity aspect of the Blessings and Curses will reinforce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T20:23:09-08:00","id":810936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=810871#post810871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna have to share a big concern: it seems the mechanics for gaining and losing Clarity reinforce bad or at least questionable behaviors. I am probably looking at it the wrong way, though. Can someone offer their own point of view?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, clarify what you mean?<br /> <br /> Second off, as it stands, Clarity is not a moral, ethical, or societal acceptance marker. It's about knowing oneself and the world as things really are as opposed to illusion and dream.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Seeming Blessings and Curses, they reassert a changeling's sense of self by letting them find solace in the actions that freed them. I suppose, using Beasts for a second here, the response of a changeling to someone complaining about fucking their mate on the table in the busy hours of the pub is &quot;Fuck you, I'm need to know again what it means to be me, on my own terms.&quot; That's the Seeming Blessings.<br /> <br /> The Curses are when something outside whispers in their mind &quot;Ah, but that's not true, is it, sweet? No matter how you try to be yourself, in the end you're what we tell you to be. You're ours, forever and always.&quot;<br /> <br /> I finished Jessica Jones last week, and while not a perfect show, you can see that conflict in Jessica a lot, and you can see the things she does to own herself, as well as the things that just happen, by chance or by Kilgrave, that destroy her sense of control, <i>of being</i>, and makes her just a puppet. You see stuff like that all over Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:33:19-08:00","id":811675,"title":"","content":"The extra Health has the advantage to speak about things that are linked to the Ogres' metaphor. Health is meat, flesh, bones, muscles. It's visceral, it's powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:37:30-08:00","id":812864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=810936#post810936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, clarify what you mean?<br /> <br /> Second off, as it stands, Clarity is not a moral, ethical, or societal acceptance marker. It's about knowing oneself and the world as things really are as opposed to illusion and dream.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Seeming Blessings and Curses, they reassert a changeling's sense of self by letting them find solace in the actions that freed them. I suppose, using Beasts for a second here, the response of a changeling to someone complaining about fucking their mate on the table in the busy hours of the pub is &quot;Fuck you, I'm need to know again what it means to be me, on my own terms.&quot; That's the Seeming Blessings.<br /> <br /> The Curses are when something outside whispers in their mind &quot;Ah, but that's not true, is it, sweet? No matter how you try to be yourself, in the end you're what we tell you to be. You're ours, forever and always.&quot;<br /> <br /> I finished Jessica Jones last week, and while not a perfect show, you can see that conflict in Jessica a lot, and you can see the things she does to own herself, as well as the things that just happen, by chance or by Kilgrave, that destroy her sense of control, <i>of being</i>, and makes her just a puppet. You see stuff like that all over Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div> I understand the gist of what you're saying. Changelings, being half-fae, would have tinges of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BlueAndOrangeMorality\" target=\"_blank\"><b>blue and orange in their morality</b></a>. I am just concerned that this new perspective will make it excessively hard for changelings to connect with non-changelings, especially mortals. I appreciate the caveat that the ways of losing and gaining Clarity specific to each Seeming happen rarely, but I would be glad and quite relieved if Clarity was defined in no uncertain terms in 2ED, so as to prevent STs and players from approaching the experience of being a changeling from the wrong direction.<br /> <br /> Was I clear enough?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:09:12-08:00","id":812883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812864#post812864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Was I clear enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, I mean, you keep saying you think it'll make it hard for changelings to connect with non-changelings and reinforce bad behaviours but you still haven't said how the new perspective will create that result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:21:30-08:00","id":812892,"title":"","content":"I think I get it, but my only response is &quot;Fairies, even formerly human ones, have trouble properly connecting to normal people? It's almost like they're fairies!&quot;<br /> <br /> Watsonian or Doylist, this is a truth of the world of fairies. They are the outsiders, and their ways are not our ways.<br /> <br /> You can never go <i>back</i>. Not really. There's only <i>forward</i>.<br /> <br /> As for Clarity itself, you want it defined in no uncertain terms to say........what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:36:20-08:00","id":812905,"title":"","content":"I admit that I may be jumping the gun with this assumption. Besides, I can imagine character concepts who keep a grip on their Clarity in ways that minimize the shock and questions of non-changelings. It's probably a &quot;feature, not bug&quot; deal.<br /> <br /> I am sorry if I'm not expressing myself adequately. I think I'll do the sensible thing and wait for the Clarity draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:00:38-08:00","id":812976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812905#post812905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit that I may be jumping the gun with this assumption. Besides, I can imagine character concepts who keep a grip on their Clarity in ways that minimize the shock and questions of non-changelings. It's probably a &quot;feature, not bug&quot; deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one I'd imagine seeming isn't the only way to improve clarity, it's just the most effective method since it ties so strongly into your fae nature (specifically, fae trying to go back to being human matching low-clarity wanting to get to high-clarity perfectly). I'd imagine that in 2e you can presumably still work hard to ground yourself and reinforce your self image in the same manner you could in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:01:58-08:00","id":813116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812864#post812864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the gist of what you're saying. Changelings, being half-fae, would have tinges of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BlueAndOrangeMorality\" target=\"_blank\"><b>blue and orange in their morality</b></a>. I am just concerned that this new perspective will make it excessively hard for changelings to connect with non-changelings, especially mortals. I appreciate the caveat that the ways of losing and gaining Clarity specific to each Seeming happen rarely, but I would be glad and quite relieved if Clarity was defined in no uncertain terms in 2ED, so as to prevent STs and players from approaching the experience of being a changeling from the wrong direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Its not exactly that Changelings have blue and orange morality, so much as that Clarity just doesn't measure morality <i>at all</i>. Clarity is a measure of a Changeling's grasp on reality. Things that call to mind their experiences in Arcadia can be traumatizing (causing Breaking Points), and like a veteran having a flashback, recalling that trauma can potentially damage their ability to discern fantasy from reality (loss of Clarity). Things that reinforce their sense of agency reassure them that they are greater than their trauma and strengthen their ability to recognize what they actually perceive versus what they merely imagine (Clarity gain).<br /> <br /> Changelings absolutely have a difficult time connecting with non-changelings, just as victims of severe trauma have a difficult time connecting with people who live relatively sheltered lives. That's one of the central parts of the drama of Changeling - you've been places and experienced things that other people just can't understand or identify with, but now you're back in the real world and one way or another, you've got to find your place in it. Fortunately, there are some others that have had similar experiences, and they can help you, but you also can't <i>only</i> associate with those people and shut yourself off from everyone else. Or rather, you can, but it wouldn't be very healthy. So you do your best to connect with other people despite the fact that it <i>is</i> excessively hard.<br /> <br /> Don't worry, from what I've seen, Clarity is extremely well-defined. I really really want to talk more about it once it's spoiled, or once the game comes out (which ever comes first) because, unless it's changed significantly since the version I've seen, it is my absolute favorite thing about 2e Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812864#post812864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was I clear enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. You're still mostly saying that you're worried the Clarity aspect of Blessings and Curses will encourage some kind of player behaviors that you perceive as negative. But you haven't really explained <i>what</i> those behaviors are or <i>why</i> you consider them negative. I've tried my best to address your concerns re: morality and relations with ordinary humans, but without understanding the specifics of what you're worried about, I can only do so in very vague terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-21-2016, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:15:50-08:00","id":813128,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812905#post812905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit that I may be jumping the gun with this assumption. Besides, I can imagine character concepts who keep a grip on their Clarity in ways that minimize the shock and questions of non-changelings. It's probably a &quot;feature, not bug&quot; deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say you're jumping the gun necessarily. If you're concerned about what you've seen so far, that concern is worth expressing sooner rather than later. This quote makes it sound like maybe you're worried about Changelings doing obviously magical things to regain Clarity? Or am I still misinterpreting you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812905#post812905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry if I'm not expressing myself adequately. I think I'll do the sensible thing and wait for the Clarity draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, but I like talking about Clarity!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T22:41:31-08:00","id":813192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812864#post812864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I would be glad and quite relieved if Clarity was defined in no uncertain terms in 2ED, so as to prevent STs and players from approaching the experience of being a changeling from the wrong direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, all of the subjective story stats have been markedly better defined and thought through in the second editions. I'd be shocked if Changeling broke from that trend, since it was always one of the stronger examples in the first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T21:06:51-08:00","id":820719,"title":"","content":"You know, I could see a Beast as a playwright or an author. The pursuit of inspiration, ones muse, or, more mundanely, the person who has inspired or can provide monitary support/publishing. Furthermore, if they want to really flaunt a rule of society, why not incorporate it into a play, poem or story?<br /> <br /> That also works well for A Beast's Burden; they could have contract obligations or deadlines, or perhaps their editor/publisher is being extra strict about their writing and either want to remove good bits or are removing the wrong parts to improve the piece. Follow the critique, or lose publishing. It's mundane, but it's quite interesting stuff when applied to these kinds of rules.<br /> <br /> It should come as no surprise to anyone here that &quot;Pendragon&quot; is a phrase that I see working quite well for a Beast, and that I have one in mind for when the game comes out naming himself &quot;Uther&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T05:28:54-08:00","id":820899,"title":"","content":"Plus, artists are known for being rather eccentric; it might help excuse some minor hiccups, from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:00:24-08:00","id":821195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=812864#post812864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ... <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BlueAndOrangeMorality\" target=\"_blank\"><b>blue and orange in their morality</b></a>. I am just concerned that this new perspective will make it excessively hard for changelings to connect with non-changelings, especially mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to paraphrase my understanding of what you are saying to be sure I understand.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally your question is something like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Aren't the socially unacceptable behaviors promoted by Seeming Blessings Clarity gain likely to result in a higher than average number of characters who pursue those behaviors to be deemed as social outcasts, dangerously mentally ill, criminal and/or outright monstrous from a sane human perspective depending on how extreme they follow those behaviors?&quot;<br /> <br /> My answer is:<br /> Many changelings are emotionally, mentally, and spiritually scarred to the point that only providence would prevent them from being social outcasts, dangerously mentally ill, criminal and/or outright monstrous from a sane human perspective. Seeming &quot;blessings&quot; reflect the damage to their psyche and souls. It, in a non-figurative sense, makes their minds unlike healthy balanced mortal minds or even like the minds of other supernatural beings who don't happen to have the exact same Seeming Blessing. This means even within 2e Changeling: the Lost what is mentally bearable/acceptable clashes in ways that cause great potential for conflict.<br /> <br /> My favorite examples involves confining a Beast for &quot;their own good&quot; or &quot;greater good&quot; with force, which is a Clarity gaining act for Darklings, Fairest, and Ogres and a Clarity break for the Beast. It is likely the Beast would view its captors as tyrants or monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-01-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:08:05-08:00","id":821234,"title":"","content":"Thumbs up, again, Pale.<br /> <br /> Adding on my impressions: It's hard being a Changeling. It's bad enough that you've got the looming danger of being abducted. The other half of the problem is that you don't fit right back into human society. To some extent, you might be &quot;playing superhero,&quot; having to make up excuses for slipping away or acting irrationally to deal with supernatural threats and courtly duties your human friends can't see. You're always the odd fellow out. If you do it badly, you're that creepy hobo people hide their kids from. If you do it well, you can pass as &quot;eccentric&quot; and maybe even oddly cool.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness 1e book, page 25. Script of a cryptozoologist describing various types of cryptids. One section is &quot;The Unearthly&quot; which sounds pretty much like a mortal description of Changelings to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:04:08-08:00","id":822475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=821195#post821195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I would like to paraphrase my understanding of what you are saying to be sure I understand.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fundamentally your question is something like this:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Aren't the socially unacceptable behaviors promoted by Seeming Blessings Clarity gain likely to result in a higher than average number of characters who pursue those behaviors to be deemed as social outcasts, dangerously mentally ill, criminal and/or outright monstrous from a sane human perspective depending on how extreme they follow those behaviors?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My answer is:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Many changelings are emotionally, mentally, and spiritually scarred to the point that only providence would prevent them from being social outcasts, dangerously mentally ill, criminal and/or outright monstrous from a sane human perspective. Seeming &quot;blessings&quot; reflect the damage to their psyche and souls. It, in a non-figurative sense, makes their minds unlike healthy balanced mortal minds or even like the minds of other supernatural beings who don't happen to have the exact same Seeming Blessing. This means even within 2e Changeling: the Lost what is mentally bearable/acceptable clashes in ways that cause great potential for conflict.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My favorite examples involves confining a Beast for &quot;their own good&quot; or &quot;greater good&quot; with force, which is a Clarity gaining act for Darklings, Fairest, and Ogres and a Clarity break for the Beast. It is likely the Beast would view its captors as tyrants or monsters.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I have mulled over your explanation and Arc's too, and I think it's clicked for me. I gotta stop approaching the 2ED Integrity and the supernatural equivalents with the lenses of 1ED Morality. Thanks for the clarification.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T20:11:22-08:00","id":823003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=822475#post822475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I have mulled over your explanation and Arc's too, and I think it's clicked for me. I gotta stop approaching the 2ED Integrity and the supernatural equivalents with the lenses of 1ED Morality. Thanks for the clarification.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If you miss having some type of karmic consequence because you harbor notions of cosmic justice as something objectively true, then let me point you to my homebrew rules which migrate and universally apply Atrocity mechanic from <i>Danse Macabre </i>as a alternative to humanity and turned it to an add-on to the Integrity/Harmony/Humanity/Wisdom/Clarity Mental Stability system to track the metaphysical weight of heinous acts of any supernatural being, and track the descent from merely being supernatural into being truly a monster.<br /> <br /> I love the nuance that the new mental stability advantages add to tracking mental stress, especially with Conditions ranging from basic fear and guilt to the depths of madness and/or being broken. They did lose the karmic justice motif, which they didn't fully reflect well anyway, since it left the descent to random dice rolls and in my play experience the most gleefully sadistic players always seemed to never fail a roll and the unlucky rube who was a nice guy most the time and got roped into cruel deeds by his psychotic motley mates always went crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-05-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T18:19:59-08:00","id":823905,"title":"","content":"I also think with the information we have that Clarity is going to be more fluid in a game session. Somewhere in between a vampire's Humanity and a werewolf's Harmony in the amount of flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T04:36:48-08:00","id":833779,"title":"","content":"Seeing as I've read up on the playtest compilation, can I make suggestions for expanding the Blessings and Curses, especially the latter (assuming said expansions will still get the green light).<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Curses</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Darkling</b>: A Darkling has been injured in the past, and believes she\u2019s injured others to survive. A Darkling trusted once, a long time ago, and anyone asking her to trust may be pushing her too hard. To trust anyone, even one\u2019s closest allies, following them blindly, causes the Darkling to suffer a Clarity break. <i>Furthermore, dice bonuses from having multiple Touchstones cap out at +3.<br /> </i><br /> <b>Fairest:</b> With measured response and skill, or blind luck and hope, making the right choice feels damn good. But sooner or later, failure weighs on the Fairest, and the crown on her head gets heavier and heavier. Any time a Fairest makes a call as a leader, and someone gets seriously hurt physically or otherwise, it is a breaking point. <i>Additionally, she suffers a -4 penalty to all breaking point rolls without any attached Touchstones.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Wizened: </b>The line between genius and perfection is thin, and the considerable talent that the Wizened has devoted himself to can also consume him. Any time a Wizened fails an action related to his unique talent, it\u2019s a breaking point. This does not have to be a roll for direct performance (and in fact, usually isn\u2019t); for example, a painter may fail in procuring a very specific pigment, and suffer, or a politician might suffer a scandal that hurts her poll numbers, or a fencer breaks her weapon on the way to a duel. <i>Failing any rolls which involve the Wizened's talent inflicts the Distracted Condition on him for a scene.</i><br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> For the Darkling and Fairest, I thought their life curse could tie into aspects of Clarity because they're both Seemings that deal heavily with people. For Darklings, it's the extent they place their trust (and are trusted by) those people they regard as their Touchstones. For Fairest, the proposed life curse should showcase how badly they can get screwed when they got no support system to help shoulder some of the burden behind their bad decisions.<br /> <br /> On the Wizened suffering the Distracted Condition, it just seems fitting. When you obsess so much on perfection, it can end up being pursued to the exclusion of everything else as they get overwhelmed in their own tunnel vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:35:35-08:00","id":840300,"title":"","content":"I also have additions/suggestions for the Ogres and Elementals in terms of Blessing and Curse. Feel free to critique on them as well.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Elemental</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Elementals are also treated as being near and/or in contact with their element for the purpose of invoking Contracts and Kith blessings.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Cold Iron also nullifies the passive benefits of the Elemental's Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Ogre</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Ogres downgrade all damage from mundane sources of harm by one level. In the case of bashing damage, they take half the amount inflicted in a turn. This blessing does not apply to damage received from deprivation, frailties, or iron.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Ogres cannot make use of Clarity-based bonuses while under the Delusional Condition. At Storyteller discretion, this can extend to similar Conditions which affect the mind and/or emotions of the changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-01-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T19:14:48-08:00","id":840325,"title":"","content":"The Playtest compiled document doesn't have some of the updated info on the Seeming Blessings like Darklings getting the ability to see in darkness or the Elemental Curse adding an extra condition when hit by iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:46:10-08:00","id":840474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=840325#post840325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Playtest compiled document doesn't have some of the updated info on the Seeming Blessings like Darklings getting the ability to see in darkness or the Elemental Curse adding an extra condition when hit by iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's presumably because it was posted in a thread and not a complete preview rather than the things that were put in the compiled document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:47:05-08:00","id":840475,"title":"","content":"I should check and see if we have the updated Seemings.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nope, not yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:07:06-08:00","id":840588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/791114-changeling-the-lost-2e-teaser-new-seeming-blessings-and-curses?p=840474#post840474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's presumably because it was posted in a thread and not a complete preview rather than the things that were put in the compiled document.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}